          "The first gap in first-day packets is usually a missing link between the source and the decision. A queue can look current while an first-day packets case is missing the form, the date, or the approval that makes it reviewable. HR Coordinators asks the team to record the source before the case moves forward. That habit separates activity from a control that a later reviewer can audit. At HR Coordinators, the first-day packets note stays with the employee file so a later HR owner can reopen it without rebuilding the history."
